course: dictionary
lesson: 1683
title: Words from church and family life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A christening is a church ceremony in which a baby is welcomed and given its name, with water on its head. Look at the clues in «A christening is a church ceremony where a baby is welcomed into the Christian church and given its names, with water on its head.» The words church, baby and welcomed tell you it is a happy event.
explain: Read the second sentence: «Godparents are chosen at a christening to take a special interest in the child as it grows.» Godparents are chosen at a church event, and they take an interest in the child as it grows. The clue is that the sentence is about a child growing up, so a christening must be the start of that.
explain: The word can also be used as a joke. If someone says «the christening of the new shoes», they mean the first time the shoes are worn. Check by swapping in the meaning: "the first time the shoes are worn" still makes sense, so the joking meaning fits.
fact: A christening is a church ceremony in which a baby is baptised and given its Christian name.
fact: At a christening, water is poured on the baby's head, and godparents are chosen to take an interest in the child.
fact: Useful phrases are «christening gown», «christening party» and «christening cake».
fact: In stories, a fairy may come to a royal christening, as in Sleeping Beauty.
fact: As a joke, a christening can mean the first use of something new, such as a ship's launch or new shoes.
exercise: «A christening is a church ceremony where a baby is welcomed into the Christian church.» What is a christening? | *A church ceremony where a baby is welcomed | A birthday party for grown-ups | A school sports day | A special kind of cake only
exercise: «Godparents are chosen at a christening to take a special interest in the child as it grows.» What do godparents do? | Sleep in the church | Cook the party food | Sell the christening gown | *Take a special interest in the child as it grows
exercise: Dad jokes, «We are having a christening party for the new shoes!» What does he mean? | The shoes are being sold in a shop | The shoes are being given away | *The shoes are being worn for the first time | The shoes are being washed in water
test: Find and copy one word from «A christening is a church ceremony where a baby is welcomed into the Christian church.» that means a formal event with set rules. | welcomed | church | *ceremony | baby
test: Which of these would you wear at a christening? | A snowsuit | A swimming cap | *A christening gown | A school uniform
exam: In the sentence «The fairy came to the royal christening», what does christening mean? | A cake shop | A kind of boat | *A church ceremony where a baby is given its name | A day for swimming
